<<~ ahu #/head>>

! A roadmap to the DreamDOM ~ from the as-built VM to the superset of cameras

''What this carrier holds.'' The build order from today's worker-thread TiddlyWiki (one engine per island, whole HTML frames to a shadow root, a render-id relay back) to the full model `dreamdom` carries: four layers, two waists, a camera as a root over a sink, a width dial, a Wiki Actor, and every surface of the superset publishing its own conformance row. Each phase names what it builds, what it proves, what it waits on, the spikes that gate it and the rulings that block it. Landed work will read in git and the CHANGELOG, never here; this carrier keeps only what stays owed, and the controller trues it as rows close.

''How it rides the house roadmap.'' `stable-founding-road#/the-attractor` names STABLE FOUNDING as the attractor and rules that ''full models land early'': a slice builds its whole model in the place the order gives it, and no slice ships a narrower interim a later slice must re-cut. This train obeys that: the camera contract lands with its per-key revisions, mount epochs, answered events and declared cancellation whole, even where its first key stays the whole surface. The train runs ''beside'' the six paths of `stable-founding-road#/the-road` on disjoint files: it touches `packages/lararium-tw5/`, `packages/lararium-web/src/projection-sink.ts`, the island protocol's wiki kinds and the house plugin, and it leaves the compose hunks of `open-node-vessel.ts` and `open-browser-vessel.ts` to their named owners, reaching them only through a module boundary and a patch to the owning lane. Where it needs a session shape (`session:surface-open`, the holder protocol), it builds against `session-contract` as ONE FACE lands it and refuses by name until then.

''The lane law binds every lane here'' (`controller-handoff#/the-lane-law`): one lead per lane in its own worktree; red first, with a control; a race pinned by the product's own event; suites from source under a scratch `HOME` and a scratch `LAR_ROOT` with `LAR_BAGS` unset; a plugin or tiddler change rebuilds the bundle in the same commit and declares its gap in `genesis/unbaked.json`; never a boot in the tracked tree; a refused command stops the lane; a burst, then one shard, then `MERGE-VERIFY`; canon lines in each commit, L-Prime kept.

''Train letter and rows.'' This train reads as ''D''. Its rows read `D1` to `D14` (#/the-rows), and its lanes read `dreamdom-<ground>`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/as-built>>

!! Where the road starts ~ the as-built, 2026-10-16

|! Piece |! Stands today |! Reads against the model |
| the third runtime | TW5 boots in a module Worker or a `worker_thread` with `$tw.browser = $tw.node = null` through one forge on both paths (the engine named by its own bytes, the CSS escape, an error reporter that surfaces and continues, every lent global non-enumerable); the core evaluates by `new Function` under a `require` allowlist and an `fs`-denying proxy; the kernel re-hashes core and plugins by CID and lends the boot shadows as tiddlers; the genesis boot harness (`packages/lararium-tw5/tests/genesis-boot.harness.ts`) boots the same bytes on either path in any suite | the ENGINE, host-neutral; the floor every host must lend |
| the store | one Automerge document per bag; island Repo ⇄ vessel Repo over a MessageChannel; a WebSocket relay adapter; a Node disk projector one way | the STORE; the store↔engine waist at record grain already stands |
| the outbound bridge | `change` → foam skip → HandGate (400 ms trailing, 2 s cap) → `bag-paths` cascade → the CRDT | the record waist's engine side; no syncer stands and none will |
| the projection | `mountProjection` renders RootTemplate plus PageStylesheet into `$tw.fakeDocument`; a 24 ms gate ships the whole story HTML and the whole CSS per change and prunes the render-id maps to the painted nodes at each flush; the page morphs into a shadow root | the browser DOM sink at width none, with one surface-wide revision, no mount epoch, no sensed revision, the CSS not yet a key of its own |
| the return leg | the patched fake `addEventListener` stamps `data-lar-rid`; the page relays click (always cancelled), a sliver of keydown, `input` and `change` as a whole value, composition guards; no event id | one third of TW5's interactions work, one third paint but act wrongly, one third have no road |
| the camera | `mountCamera(engine, {rootTiddler, document, container})` takes `window.document` or a fake document | the camera as root plus sink already stands as code |
| the confirm road | `$:/temp/confirm/*`, `tm-confirm`, `$dialog`; wired and tested; a fork-only `startup/confirm.js` | one parked question, one answer, one re-dispatch, across the superset |
| authority | the wiki island's capability check answers `worker-trust`; a second tab refuses without `?holder` and then shares one fake DOM | the actor's manifest and gate stay owed |
| the daemon surface | `tm-verse-event` → `placeVerb`; summoned by Ctrl+Shift+D or ☰ | the daemon actor, always awake |
| the filter and render ask | none on the live island; the one such surface stands orphaned | the port's `ask` kinds, owed |

The ranked gaps behind this table (the textarea revert #23, the blanket `preventDefault` #1, checkbox and radio and select #4, the root `tm-*` services #2, the frozen pane on switch #13) stand in `docs/pono/tw5-vm-gaps-scout` §4 and §5; `dreamdom#/what-a-sink-keeps` carries the six silent losses and their cures. The cold read of the ground D0 mended stands verbatim at `dreamdom-harness-scout`; the field read for D0 and D1 at `dreamdom-field-scout`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-attractor>>

!! The attractor ~ what "done" reads as

The train closes when ''every surface of the superset publishes a row'' (`dreamdom#/the-superset`): its width, its root and sink, the control kinds and service kinds its manifest carries, and its result against the three conformance families (`filter-cts`, the camera goldens, the interaction goldens) with a named refusal wherever it has no road. Along the way:

* the first surface (the browser on the Node vessel's box) shows the daemon wiki, the pinned wiki and the other wikis as recipes or sleeping actors, and spawns each as the ordinary page template at the width the spike ruled;
* the browser DOM sink at width none loses no person's work: the six silent losses each pin to a green golden;
* one engine per wiki lives as an actor with a manifest, hibernates and wakes with its attachments, and refuses by name what its manifest lacks;
* a lean host (Mudlet, MCP) reads keys and writes records, and every act comes back named;
* the suite runs per host, and host drift (`Intl`, `localeCompare`, `Date`) shows on a published row before an operator meets it.

''Off the attractor by ruling'' (#/off-this-road): the syncer, the mutators, any authority on either side, a second evaluator, live 3D before the sensorium, UE6 before early access.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-order>>

!! The order ~ eight phases, one train

''The organizing law.'' The camera contract lands before any glass engine, so width none stays an honest fallback on every host; the record port lands before the glass engine, so the glass has records to replicate; the spike runs before the default width gets ruled; the actor wraps what stands rather than preceding it; conformance rides beside everything from D1 on, and no surface counts as landed without a row.

''The order'': D0 → D1 → D2 → D3 → D4, with D5 beside D1 onward and D6 after D2 and D5; D7 held by name.

!!! D0 · MEASURE AND MEND ~ what every phase needs (lane `dreamdom-harness`; the harness, the engine mends and the worker-side baseline stand; the rest stays owed here)
* ''Owed'': the two browser-side baselines, a stock tab over the reference corpus reading `mainRender`, `styleRefresh` and `mainRefresh` and a long-animation-frames observer on the current page (Chromium alone carries the observer; `dreamdom-field-scout` §6), beside the worker-side numbers `pnpm --filter @lararium/tw5 measure:frames` derives; a second boot writing nothing, pinned over a staged vessel in e2e. A burr for D3's spike: TiddlyWiki's `utils.timer` reads `window.performance` wherever `$tw.node` stands null, so `$:/config/Performance/Instrumentation` throws in the island until the forge lends a timer.
* ''Waits on'': nothing. ''Spikes'': none; this phase IS the instrument. ''Rulings'': none.

!!! D1 · THE CAMERA CONTRACT ~ the browser DOM sink at width none, hardened (lane `dreamdom-camera`; waits on D0's harness)
* ''Builds'', whole: keyed frames with a per-key revision, a `membership` key, a `mountEpoch` and `sensedRevision[controlId]`, one whole-surface key first and the CSS as a key of its own (so a sheet crosses only when it changes, and the vessel's frame relay carries an absent key as absent); `wiki:control-event` with `eventId`, `kind`, `seenFrameRev`, `localRev`, `wholeValue`, `modifiers`, `key` and as-of-act `geometry`; `projection:control-result` with `applied` · `stale-target` · `refused` and `want`; the answer ring per surface; declared cancellation and crossing (`data-lar-on`, `data-lar-cancel`, `data-lar-keys`, `data-lar-bubble`, `data-lar-live` descriptors) stamped by the patched `addEventListener` and a small per-widget table; the worker bubbling every type to the first listener and answering `unclaimed`; the serialiser promoting `checked` and `selected` to attributes at flush; `projection:resend` on `session:surface-open` and on switch; the island root-services startup module (`tm-rename-tiddler`, `tm-relink-tiddler`, `tm-home`, `tm-modal`, `tm-show-switcher`, `tm-notify`, `tm-scroll` and `tm-focus-selector` as hints) and `glass:service` with `service-result` for clipboard, download, route and open-surface, each other kind refused by name with its alert; the three ruled page controls (`lar-field` through the editor's engine seam, `lar-popover`, `lar-disclosure`) and the page's per-control veto in `beforeNodeMorphed`; the IME rules (`keyCode 229`, one-task hold after `compositionend`, never morph a composing node); `lar-file-picker` and the page-side `import-offer` and `drop` with bounded bytes; `lar-order-list`; the document keyboard leg driven by a `shortcuts` key; the navigate service with the page composing `#` from the order key.
* ''Proves'': interaction goldens 1 to 13 (`dreamdom#/conformance`) green at width none over the DOM sink in Playwright, each red first; the five probes of `page-controls#/measure-first`; the three faults of `page-controls#/the-sink-today` closed; `glass-switch-back-repaints`; `glass-print-refuses-by-name`; the refusal words of `page-controls#/refusals` read beside the control in each engine.
* ''Measures'': serialised bytes per key and long animation frames across 100 edits beside the 11.7 KB plus 7.5 KB whole-frame number; a key splits (river frames plus order plus membership) only where that number asks (`dreamdom#/the-ruling`, measure first).
* ''Waits on'': D0's harness; `session-contract#/the-holder-protocol` for the envelope fields (builds against it; refuses `binding-unavailable` where a field has no holder yet).
* ''Spikes'': the declared-cancellation afternoon (#/the-spikes 1), serializer promotion (2), sensed revision end to end (3), the seam engine's toolbar (4), declared keys and the document leg (5), `import-offer` and `drop` (6), surface switch with epochs (7).
* ''Rulings'': the edit template of the browser DOM sink (`dreamdom#/open-rulings` 8); the root `tm-*` split and the `tm-http-request` gate (9); `$eventcatcher` and `$keyboard` (10). Each blocks only its rows; the rest of the phase lands around them.

!!! D2 · THE RECORD PORT ~ inside the engine (lane `dreamdom-port`; its pure steps start beside D1)
* ''Builds'': the port's kinds on the live island: `port:open{wikiUri, width, since, actor, localFilter, renders[], edits, presence, maxRecordBytes, maxBatchBytes}`, `port:snapshot` (chunked), `port:changes` with cursors and tombstones, `port:write{txId, basis, records}` answered by `port:written` and echoed under `causedBy:[txId]`, `port:ask{kind: filter · render · load · verb · cas · invoke}` where `render` answers `html` · `text` · `blocks` (with `affordances[]`) · `label-html` and `invoke` carries a `renderCursor`, `port:presence` (30 s expiry, never persisted), `port:close`; the width field as a filter over fields on the engine side (cheap now, expensive to retrofit); the tier `localFilter` naming StoryList, HistoryList, `$:/state`, `$:/temp`, `$:/status` and `$:/info/browser/*`; a recording fakedom-style document and the blocks, text and label-html serialisers over it; the capability gate on every invoke before `invokeActions`; the orphaned `meme-worker-script.ts` retired.
* ''Proves'': `port-echo-named-by-txid`, `port-presence-expires`, `port-skinny-then-load`, `port-storylist-stays-local`, `ask-render-label-html-is-qt-subset`, `ask-render-text-keeps-links-as-handles`, `ask-invoke-stale-cursor-refused`, `non-admin-invoke-refused`; the blocks-sink parity run of interaction goldens 1, 2, 6 and 11 (headless, vitest) with the same expected writes and messages as the DOM sink; a missing camera degrades visibly.
* ''Waits on'': D0. The serialisers wait on nothing; `blocks` for memetic-wikitext specifically waits on the Annex B widget-tree pass (D5).
* ''Spikes'': the blocks sink over a recording document (#/the-spikes 8); the synchronous ask on Node (`Atomics.wait` plus `receiveMessageOnPort`, bounded waits only).
* ''Rulings'': the presence lane's home at width none (`dreamdom#/open-rulings` 12). The port ships with `causedBy` mandatory and skinny behind a flag, as the v2 plan proposed; the operator may still rule either way without re-cutting.

!!! D3 · THE GLASS ENGINE AND THE WIDTH SPIKE ~ full, skinny and story behind a flag (lane `dreamdom-glass`; waits on D1 and D2)
* ''Builds'': a port adaptor as a startup module on the glass that binds `$tw.wiki`'s `change` event, lands `port:changes` under an origin tag its own listener skips, posts `port:write` with `txId` and keeps the write optimistic until `port:written` echoes; no `$tw.syncer` constructed and no `syncadaptor` module shipped; the glass boot from the same CAS core blob by hash; the page template over `window.document` mounted in-process as the browser's first camera; skinny and story as settings of the same adaptor; `glass:service` doors reached from the glass engine's root handlers; the multi-tab topology (a Web Lock elects the leader, the leader's worker holds the engine, a SharedWorker or a BroadcastChannel handshake routes other tabs, a late tab gets a snapshot and never a missed `ready`); peer write into an open draft shown with the newer-base prompt; `§9` of `packages/AGENTS.md` reworded on the operator's ruling.
* ''Proves'': the full-width walk of the five `isTiddlyWikiFakeDom` sites in a real browser (`FramedEngine` inside the shadow root, storyviews, popup positioning, the toolbar, auto-height) before any default gets ruled; `glass-peer-edit-presence-reads-aloud`, `glass-skinny-body-loads-on-open`, `glass-echo-lands-once`, `glass-leader-handoff-mid-write`, `glass-late-tab-gets-snapshot`; interaction goldens 1 to 13 at width full with stock TW5 as oracle, which also certifies the goldens themselves.
* ''Measures'' (the separating experiment): one 2,000-tiddler corpus, one loopback port, the same glass booted at full, skinny and none (story only if skinny and full split), on the reference phone and on Node: heap after first paint; warm first paint; p95 keystroke-to-paint; the cold filter over tiddlers the glass never held; the peer write into the open editor; echo (exactly one write, zero re-landings); hot-swap to a second wiki and back; the synchronous ask on Node; the verb census (every worker-side verb that invoked a filter or a render); bytes per key at none. Thresholds: skinny loses if the cold filter exceeds 100 ms p95 on the phone or a `lazy-all` hole reproduces without a closable fix; full loses only on the marginal-memory gate (+25 % over a stock tab; a 150 MB tripwire); none loses if bytes per key exceed the 50 ms input budget on the phone after the key split, or if any ruled control fails its browser and accessibility probes.
* ''Waits on'': D1 (so none stands as the honest fallback) and D2 (so the glass has a port).
* ''Spikes'': the three-boot width spike (#/the-spikes 9); the full-width walk (10).
* ''Rulings'': the default width of the first surface (`dreamdom#/open-rulings` 1); the `§9` wording (2); the confirm road's home per width (6). The flag ships before the rulings; the default flips after.

!!! D4 · THE WIKI ACTOR ~ the lifecycle layer (lane `dreamdom-actor`; waits on D2; its manifest and gate may start beside D3)
* ''Builds'': one actor per wiki with an id, one writer and a manifest `{renders[], edits, presence, sensoria[], width[], maxRecordBytes, maxBatchBytes}`; the capability gate on the actor replacing `worker-trust` (admin-auth plus the keyhive check over `requestedBy`), so a lean invoke never bypasses authority; the states daemon · pinned · sleeping · recipe · spawned with their transitions; per-port attachments `{cursor, subscriptions, width, actorKey, localFilter, cameraMount}` serialised at hibernation and restored at wake; wake-on-act with one parked act per surface and a `waking` state beside the control, `superseded` for a second act, `actor-not-spawned` with a `spawn` affordance for a recipe; the holder's refusal to hibernate an actor holding an unanswered reliable act; the first surface's list of wikis by state; `tm-open-window` as `open-surface` (a second camera on the same actor); `$:/state` per surface or shared, by ruling; a warm start measured against `v8.startupSnapshot` in a `worker_thread`.
* ''Proves'': `actor-hibernates-with-two-ports-and-both-resume`, `third-port-during-hibernation-wakes`, `percept-without-sensoria-cap-refused-by-name`, `wake-on-act-answers-parked-act`, `recipe-link-refuses-with-spawn`, `hibernate-refused-while-reliable-act-pending`, `sense-never-blocks-hibernation`; interaction golden 14; the blur test as a witness: a glass that cannot hand back its attachment and resume reads red.
* ''Waits on'': D2 (attachments name port state); the session contract's surface-open for the manifest handshake.
* ''Spikes'': hibernate and wake (#/the-spikes 11); hibernate mid-edit (12).
* ''Rulings'': the actor manifest shape (`dreamdom#/open-rulings` 5); wake on act (7); `$:/state` per surface (11).

!!! D5 · CONFORMANCE ~ three families, every host a row (lane `dreamdom-suite`; rides beside D1 onward on disjoint files)
* ''Builds'': `filter-cts.json` for the house filter dialect, generated from the pinned JS engine over a frozen world (`worlds/pono-small`), reviewed once, tagged (`core`, `host-bound`, `set`, `fault`, `since`, `strange`), near 250 tests; the camera goldens at `html` and `text` keyed by (root template, serialiser); the Annex B widget-tree pass (`resolveWidgetTree(ast, registry)`) and then the `blocks` golden, with `label-html` derived from `blocks` through a declared projection; the interaction goldens' `interaction/` section with its fourteen scripts and a script runner that speaks the contract's vocabulary for Playwright, vitest and (later) a Lua and an MCP harness; the suite run on three hosts from day one (Node, a browser, quickjs-ng) with a skip list by name per host; the `since` pin to the TW5 fork commit and the parity discipline (a drifting hash names a disagreement, never a content edit).
* ''Proves'': the suite itself green on the reference engine on each host; host drift shows as a named skip (`Intl` on quickjs-ng first); a port that lags the pinned commit fails by lag, not by wrong code; a specimen's `html` golden stays byte-stable across two hosts.
* ''Waits on'': nothing for `filter-cts` and the `html`/`text` goldens; D1 for the interaction goldens to run at none; D3 for them to run at full; D2 for the blocks run.
* ''Spikes'': `filter-cts.json` (#/the-spikes 13); the Annex B pass (14).
* ''Rulings'': interaction goldens blessed as a family (`dreamdom#/open-rulings` 13); the `core` charter and oracle ownership (14).

!!! D6 · THE LEAN SINKS ~ the surfaces without an engine in the app (lane `dreamdom-lean`; waits on D2 and D5's `blocks` golden)
* ''Builds'': the ''Node CLI'' text camera over the port (`lares act … --yes` as acts, writes from files, asks for filters and renders); the ''SSR face'' (RootTemplate or a static template through the fakedom camera, links as real `href` routes, forms as writes or acts over the holder, a surface attaching for live mode); the ''MCP projection'' (resources ↔ keys with a cursor in the annotations, `subscribe` and `updated` ↔ `port:changes` without payload, `tools/call` per affordance kind, elicitation for the confirm road and `lar-field` schemas, `tools/list_changed` when the affordance set changes, the suite's `fault` names as the tool's error vocabulary); the ''Mudlet weekend'' (a loopback telnet listener in the node island with GMCP, NAWS and CHARSET negotiation and MCCP refused, the `Lar.*` package family mirroring the port kinds, chunking at ~2 KB with a `part/of` envelope, then the `lar.mpackage` with Geyser panes painted from `label-html` keys, a `Geyser.TextEdit` save round-tripping a `txId`, an affordance click invoking by id, a refusal painting an alert); later the proxy mode with GMCP tee (`Room.Info` and `Char.Items` to records, vitals to presence, the river to a log beside the island and never the CRDT); squads only after a wizard grant exists (a keyhive grant, per-character sockets, a reflex table, an intent verb, `squad/*` tiddlers, a game-visible tag, an audit log).
* ''Proves'': `gmcp-handshake-will-do`, `gmcp-snapshot-chunks-reassemble`, `gmcp-write-txid-echo-named`, `gmcp-presence-expires-30s`, `gmcp-oversize-record-refused-by-name`, `pkg-renders-title-on-open`, `pkg-textedit-save-roundtrips-txid`, `pkg-affordance-click-invokes`, `pkg-refusal-paints-alert`, `proxy-passthrough-bytes-identical`, `proxy-river-not-in-crdt`, `proxy-mccp-refused-by-name`; the MCP projection's rows for interaction goldens 1, 2, 11 and 14 with elicitation as the confirm road; each lean surface's published row with its refusals by name.
* ''Waits on'': D2 (the port and the serialisers); D5's `blocks` golden for parity; the operator's Mudlet rulings.
* ''Spikes'': the Mudlet weekend (#/the-spikes 15).
* ''Rulings'': Mudlet's first carrier and its MCP `lua` tool (`dreamdom#/open-rulings` 15); the river's home, vitals as presence, squad consent artefacts, the package namespace and the minimum Mudlet version (`mudlet-scout`).

!!! D7 · THE WIDER SURFACES ~ held by name until their gates open
* ''QuickJS, quickjs-ng and Hermes shells'': the engine runs here (ES2020 core, pump-mode timers where no `setTimeout`), the host supplies the sink (a React Native view tree as a blocks projection with the platform's own event-count handshake on `TextInput`); the store needs Automerge lent natively through host functions or a neighbour that holds it. Gate: a native Automerge adapter, unbuilt in this house; the Node-backend PuerTS probe first because it sidesteps the split. Rides the suite's host rows (D5).
* ''The UE6 and Verse sidecar'': a blocks sink to Scene Graph entities and UMG panels over `IWebSocket`, affordance invokes with the player as actor, edits as whole-value writes. Gate: UE6 early access (announced for late 2027); nothing public says Verse will host a long-lived VM or that UE6 embeds a JS engine; UE5 through PuerTS stands as the bounded probe. No work before early access.
* ''The canvas camera'': a canvas root over a DOM-hosting document with one transform per layer, keyed by shape, `sense` carrying shape geometry as absolute snapshots; the object budget (~500 live, ~4000 ceiling) measured on the best shipped implementation before trusting either; TLDraw studied, never depended on (`wikispace-canvasspace-ontology#/the-surface-law`). Gate: D1's keyed contract and D5's `blocks` golden; a rasterising shortcut refuses.
* ''Other browsers and WebView shells'': the same two members as the first surface, storage named evictable (Tauri, iOS WKWebView) and a native-FS adapter shipped from day one. Rides D3.
* ''VS Code and Obsidian, Foundry VTT, Owlbear Rodeo, editors and bots'': each a port adapter over the one port, never a bespoke protocol; any adapter that needs a new kind proposes it to the port, not to its host. Community lanes after D6.
* ''The sensorium's gate'': percepts arrive as writes or verbs with the river as actor through the capability the vessel declared; live 3D games (a video frame stream, a perception model at interactive rates, a sub-100 ms actuator loop) wait on the sensorium finishing (operator, 2026-10-16). Not researched further here.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-spikes>>

!! The spikes ~ each gating a phase, each a day to a week, each outside the tracked tree

# ''Declared cancellation in one afternoon'' (D1): the `data-lar-on` and `data-lar-cancel` table for `$link`, `$button`, `$keyboard`, `$dropzone`, `$droppable`, `$browse`, `$checkbox`, `$radio`, `$select`, `$edit-text`, `$range`; click bubbling to the first listener with `unclaimed`; Playwright: an external link opens, a native checkbox toggles, the file picker opens.
# ''Serializer promotion'' (D1): `checked` and `selected` properties to attributes at flush; the radio paints, the select holds.
# ''Sensed revision end to end'' (D1): `localRev` on `sense`, `sensedRevision` in the frame, the `beforeNodeMorphed` veto; type, hold the answer, deliver an older frame, read the value, caret, focus, undo and the wiki's field; under focus, blur, composition and a `<select>`.
# ''The seam engine's toolbar'' (D1): render the stock toolbar through the third engine, run all ten text operations over a carried pair, list which refuse `selection-unavailable`.
# ''Declared keys and the document leg'' (D1): `data-lar-keys` from `parseKeyDescriptors`, real `key` and `code`, a `shortcuts` key; search Enter, tag-picker Enter, one global shortcut.
# ''`import-offer` and `drop`'' (D1): page-side parse of `text/vnd.tiddler`, bounded bytes, `$:/Import` parks and performs.
# ''Surface switch with epochs'' (D1): `projection:resend`, `mountEpoch` on acts, an act with an old epoch answers `stale-target`.
# ''A blocks sink over a recording document'' (D2): a ~400-line document implementation that records nodes and bound listeners; render the teacher fixture's `GettingStarted` and one `$list`-bearing tiddler to `blocks`, `text` and `label-html`; a missing camera degrades visibly; interaction goldens 1, 2, 6 and 11 at parity with the DOM sink.
# ''The three-boot width spike'' (D3; the separating experiment of `docs/pono/third-ways-scout` §10): one corpus, one loopback port, widths full, skinny and none, the measures and thresholds of D3 above; the fourth boot, story, only if skinny and full split.
# ''The full-width walk of the five sites'' (D3): the glass engine over `window.document` inside the shadow root; `FramedEngine`, storyviews, popup positioning, the toolbar and auto-height each exercised once in a real browser before the default width gets ruled.
# ''Hibernate and wake'' (D4): an actor with two attached ports hibernates, wakes, both resume at their cursors with their widths and mounts; a third port opened during hibernation triggers the wake; a port without `sensoria` sending a percept reads `refused: cap sensoria`.
# ''Hibernate mid-edit'' (D4): an actor with a parked act refuses to hibernate; a `sense` never blocks it; wake answers the parked act.
# ''`filter-cts.json`'' (D5): generated from the JS engine over a frozen world, reviewed once, tagged; run on Node, in a browser and in quickjs-ng so host drift shows on day one.
# ''The Annex B widget-tree pass'' (D5): `resolveWidgetTree(ast, registry)` for memetic-wikitext, so the `blocks` golden has something to render through.
# ''The Mudlet weekend'' (D6): a loopback telnet listener, `Lar.*` packages, one Geyser label painted from a `label-html` key, one `Geyser.TextEdit` save round-tripping a `txId`.

Every spike runs under a scratch `LAR_ROOT` with `LAR_BAGS` unset, boots nothing in the tracked tree, and hands back its numbers as a row in the phase's handback; a spike that would move genesis bytes stops and reports which bytes move.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-rulings>>

!! The rulings this road waits on ~ the operator's, each beside the phase it blocks

The full list with its options stands at `dreamdom#/open-rulings`; this table names only what each blocks, so the controller brings the operator the right question at the right moment and builds around the rest.

|! Ruling |! Blocks |! Until then |
| the edit template of the browser DOM sink | D1's editor rows | the seam engine renders the stock template; `lar-field` under `$edit-text` |
| the root `tm-*` split and the `tm-http-request` gate | D1's services rows | the proposed split; `tm-http-request` refused |
| `$eventcatcher` and `$keyboard` at width none | D1's keyboard rows | `$eventcatcher` REFUSED; `$keyboard` with declared keys |
| the presence lane's home at width none | D2 | a separate droppable message |
| the default width of the first surface | D3's default flip | the flag; none as fallback |
| `§9` of `packages/AGENTS.md`, re-read as no //truth// on the main thread | D3's glass engine | the glass lands behind the flag and the wording lands with the ruling |
| the confirm road's home per width | D3 | per actor in the worker at none; per tab on the glass engine |
| the actor manifest shape | D4 | the proposed shape with `sensoria[]` as planes |
| wake on act | D4 | wake, bounded, with `superseded` |
| `$:/state` per surface at width none | D4's multi-tab rows | shared, as the confirm road rules for one question |
| the interaction goldens as a family | D5 | the fourteen scripts stand as proposed |
| the `core` charter and oracle ownership | D5's host rows | `core` as the hybrid charter names it; the lane re-pours |
| Mudlet's first carrier and its MCP `lua` tool | D6's Mudlet rows | the virtual-MUD listener; the `lua` tool off |
| the moʻolelo | nothing | the draft stands marked |

A ruling reaches the operator only where its answer changes who holds authority, custody at rest or identity bytes and no ruling settles it; otherwise the controller takes the house reading named in the third column, marks it, and builds (`controller-handoff#/the-seat`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-rows>>

!! The rows ~ one line per open loop, beside the phase that closes it

* `D1` The browser-side baselines (a stock tab, a long-animation-frames observer) and the second-boot-writes-nothing pin over a staged vessel. D0. Nobody owes a ruling.
* `D2` Per-key revisions, membership, mount epoch and sensed revision in `projection:frame`; the three faults of `page-controls#/the-sink-today` closed. D1.
* `D3` `wiki:control-event` with an id and `projection:control-result` with a status; the answer ring; the reliable and droppable classes. D1.
* `D4` Declared cancellation, crossing keys and bubbling stamped at binding; the serializer promotion; the textarea revert, the blanket cancel and the toggle family green. D1. Rulings 8 and 10 for their rows.
* `D5` The island root-services module and `glass:service` with named refusals; `projection:resend` and epochs on switch. D1. Ruling 9.
* `D6` The three ruled page controls built and probed in each engine; `lar-file-picker`, `lar-order-list`, the IME rules, the navigate service. D1.
* `D7` The port's kinds on the live island with `causedBy`, width, the tier filter and the capability gate on invoke; the recording document and its three serialisers. D2. Ruling 12.
* `D8` The glass port adaptor behind a flag, the multi-tab leader, the full-width walk of the five sites. D3. Rulings 2 and 6.
* `D9` The three-boot spike's numbers and the default width. D3. Ruling 1 (operator).
* `D10` The actor's manifest, gate, states, attachments, wake-on-act and recipe refusal; `worker-trust` retired. D4. Rulings 5, 7 and 11.
* `D11` `filter-cts.json` reviewed and pinned; the `html` and `text` goldens on three hosts. D5. Ruling 14.
* `D12` The Annex B pass and the `blocks` golden; `label-html` derived. D5.
* `D13` The interaction goldens' runner and section, green at none, full and blocks. D5. Ruling 13.
* `D14` The CLI text camera, the SSR face, the MCP projection and the Mudlet weekend, each with a published row. D6. Ruling 15 (operator).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/off-this-road>>

!! Off this road, by ruling

* ''The TW5 syncer and any syncadaptor facade'' (operator, 2026-10-16); ''mutation-log and DOM-delta streams'' (operator); ''either side authoritative''; ''the store-only worker as sole engine''; ''the lockstep twin'': each named once at `dreamdom#/the-rejected` and re-argued nowhere.
* ''A second full evaluator'' of TW5 wikitext or filters in any language; a certified `core` subset stays permitted and unscheduled until a host proves an offline need (`evaluators-one-or-many`).
* ''Live 3D games'' wait on the sensorium finishing; ''UE6'' waits on early access; both recorded in D7 and researched no further here.
* ''Web2 systems'' (Cloudflare, Discord's gateway, Foundry's socket.io) carry bytes or projections only, behind a causal-island boundary; the store never models them.
* ''A rasterising canvas'' refuses under the surface law; a vendor's licence never enters the camera.
* ''The operator's own founding'' and the two-hearth ceremony stay the operator's hands (`stable-founding-road#/the-road`); this train founds nothing.

<<~/ahu>>

